<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keserwan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kisrawan, Kesrouan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keserwan is a mountainous district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lebanon">Mount Lebanon</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a>, inhabited mainly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maronites">Maronite Christians</a>. From the 17th century it was dominated by the Khazen sheikhs under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> of Mount <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>. In 1858 its peasants rose against their lords and set up a short-lived peasant government, an episode that preceded the civil war of 1860.</p></div>
